.TH QLOGO 1 "November 2, 2026" "QLogo @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qlogo \- UCBLogo-compatible Logo interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qlogo
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fISCRIPT\fR] [\fB\-\fR [\fIARGUMENT\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qlogo
is a compiler and interpreter for the UCBLogo language.
An optional
.I SCRIPT
is run before the prompt.
Words after a lone
.B \-
are placed in the Logo variable
.B COMMAND.LINE
and are not parsed as options.
.PP
On a terminal,
.B qlogo
uses a text interface.
Redirected input and output use a plain stream instead.
Inside the language, the
.B HELP
command prints documentation for a primitive or library procedure.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-libloc " file"
Read the standard library from
.I file
instead of the installed library database.
.TP
.BI \-\-helploc " file"
Read help text from
.I file
instead of the installed help database.
.TP
.BI \-\-cslsloc " directory"
Read Computer Science Logo Style programs from
.I directory
instead of the installed
.B csls
directory.
The
.B CSLS
environment variable sets the same path when this option is absent.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Use the text interface.
This requires a terminal, and it is the default when both standard input
and standard output are terminals.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tui
Use the plain stream interface even on a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-Psychi
Reserved for the
.BR psychi (1)
graphical environment.
Do not use it from a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-\-verifyIR ", " \-\-showCON ", " \-\-traceEvaluator
Print interpreter debugging information.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/startup.lg
Logo file loaded automatically at startup, if it exists.
.TP
.I @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_DATADIR@/qlogo/qlogo_library.db
Standard library. Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 only.
.TP
.I @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_DATADIR@/qlogo/qlogo_help.db
Help text shown by
.BR HELP .
Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 only.
.TP
.I @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_DATADIR@/qlogo/csls/
Logo programs loaded by the
.B CSLSLOAD
command.
Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 only.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR psychi (1)
